{"recordingLink":"https://youtube.com/unlisted/gridsense-founder-statement-thandeka","statement":"I spent six years as a grid-data analyst at Eskom, working directly with the load-shedding stage-scheduling systems that our national schedule is built on. I watched, from the inside, how a suburb-level schedule gets published and how badly it can diverge from what actually happens on a specific street — because I was often the one fielding the escalations when it did.

My mother has run a spaza shop in Soweto for over 15 years, and I grew up watching her lose stock and money guessing wrong on generator timing, exactly the problem GridSense solves. I'm not approaching this as an outsider building an app for "the township market" in the abstract — I have the technical grid-data background to know exactly where the official schedule fails, and the lived family experience to know exactly what that failure costs a real business owner, in rand, every month.

That combination — insider knowledge of how Eskom's own scheduling data is built and where it breaks down, plus direct family exposure to the cost of that breakdown — is why I'm building this rather than someone else."}

{"members":[{"name":"Thandeka Founder","role":"CEO & Founder","linkedin":"https://linkedin.com/in/thandeka-gridsense"},{"name":"Bongani Technical","role":"Contract Android Developer (part-time)","linkedin":"https://linkedin.com/in/bongani-dev"}],"gaps":"Honest gap: we do not yet have a full-time technical co-founder. Bongani is a part-time contract Android developer (10 hours/week) who built the current pilot app; this is the single biggest team risk and the top use of the CP16 raise — hiring a full-time technical co-founder or senior engineer within the first 6 months. We also don't yet have a dedicated sales/partnerships hire, which currently means Thandeka personally runs all spaza-association outreach — this won't scale past roughly 50 businesses without a dedicated hire.

Advisors: no formal advisory board yet — this is also a gap. We've had informal input from a former Yoco regional partnerships lead on the association go-to-market model, but no signed advisory agreement exists yet.

Complementary skills: Thandeka's Eskom grid-data background covers the prediction/product logic; Bongani covers the mobile engineering execution. Neither of us has formal sales or fundraising experience, which is the second-most-honest gap in this team."}

